#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=13 nAlgorithms=8;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1787719393752'; [Wed Aug 26 06:43:13 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.), (Hayamizu et al, 2026 ; M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation).
The original input consisted of 257 taxa and 257 DNA sequences of length 444.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options, except RandomRestarts=100) so as to obtain 302 nodes and 328 edges.
The Median Joining method (Bandelt et al 1999) was used (default options) so as to obtain 281 nodes and 291 edges.
The Stretch Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 302 nodes and 328 edges.

References:
Bandelt et al 1999: HJ Bandelt, P. Forster, and A. Röhl. Median-joining networks for inferring intraspecific phylogenies. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 16:37–48, 1999.
Hayamizu et al, 2026: M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

